Well, well, well. Looks like the old ''}
Mr. Johnson who's been living behind those chipped paint and faded curtains is not as tight on funds as he's been letting on. Who would've guessed? A Lamborghini parked in the garage, covered up like a spy's getaway car. And that fishing boat down at the marina—turns out it's his, too. Little miss busybody from next door couldn’t keep it to herself, not with a secret this juicy. 

I figure, maybe he just likes to keep it hush-hush. Keeps the riff-raff away, you know? Me, I’m not one to pry, but if someone needed a little encouragement to loosen their lips, I know a guy. Or maybe, just maybe, this could be the angle I’ve been looking for to finally close this month’s books with a few extra zeros. The city’s a big, dark place, but sometimes, just sometimes, a little light sneaks in.
